From bb26588477f71396768d1ae674d63fb180c709d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:44:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] package the licence of the statically linked Skia

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; every skia-pathops wheel on PyPI has the same gap, so it needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

pathops._pathops links libskia.a (built from the skia-builder submodule)
statically, so every wheel carries Skia's BSD-3-Clause code, whose
licence requires the copyright notice to travel with binary
redistributions. setup.cfg's `license_file = LICENSE` replaces
setuptools' default licence glob, so the wheel ships skia-pathops' own
LICENSE alone.

Name both files in license_files; setuptools keeps the path, so Skia's
lands as dist-info/licenses/src/cpp/skia-builder/skia/LICENSE.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index a2d8121..d0657b3 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -2,4 +2,6 @@
 formats = zip
 
 [metadata]
-license_file = LICENSE
+license_files =
+    LICENSE
+    src/cpp/skia-builder/skia/LICENSE
-- 
2.43.0

